# `[string]` is the TYPE spelling; a value needs `[]string`. The old message was
# "expected an expression" -- true, and useless for the guess everyone makes
# first. ROADMAP.md rates the typed empty a learning-curve item rather than a
# language gap; a message that names both working forms is what turns a
# learning-curve item into a one-time mistake.
#
# Restricted to primitive type KEYWORDS, which can never be an expression:
# `[Foo]` stays a one-element array literal of a variable named Foo.
fn main():
    xs := [string]
    push(xs, "a")
    println(str(len(xs)))
